<!-- Main Content Container (Single Top-to-Bottom Flow) -->
<div class="container main-content about-page-wrapper">
    <header class="page-header">
        <h1>About Heritage-Blog</h1>
        <p>A production-ready, full-stack server-rendered blogging platform built from scratch.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="about-card">
        <section class="about-section">
            <h3>Project Overview & Vision</h3>
            <p>
                <strong>Heritage-Blog</strong> is a robust, custom-built web application engineered using Node.js, Express, and EJS. Designed as a complete full-stack portfolio project, it moves away from managed BaaS solutions to maintain absolute control over server-side architecture, custom routing, middleware layers, database schemas, and data security workflows.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="about-section">
            <h3>Core Features Implemented</h3>
            
            <div class="feature-category">
                <h4>1. Authentication & Security</h4>
                <ul class="tech-list">
                    <li><strong>Secure Auth:</strong> JWT-based authentication stored securely in HTTP-only cookies with protected route middleware.</li>
                    <li><strong>Credential Protection:</strong> Password hashing via bcrypt and unique username/email validation.</li>
                    <li><strong>Account Verification & Recovery:</strong> Email verification using OTPs sent via Nodemailer (with 5-minute expiration), alongside complete forgot-password and password-reset workflows.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="feature-category">
                <h4>2. Profile & Media Management</h4>
                <ul class="tech-list">
                    <li><strong>Cloud Storage Integration:</strong> Profile picture uploads managed via Multer and stored remotely on Cloudinary, with public IDs tracked in MongoDB.</li>
                    <li><strong>Lifecycle Cleanup:</strong> Automatic removal of temporary server-side files post-upload.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="feature-category">
                <h4>3. Blog Post Lifecycle (CRUD)</h4>
                <ul class="tech-list">
                    <li><strong>Ownership-Protected Operations:</strong> Users can create, view, edit, and delete their own blog posts, backed by strict ownership checks linked through the User model.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="feature-category">
                <h4>4. Architecture & Tech Stack</h4>
                <ul class="tech-list">
                    <li><strong>Server & Templating:</strong> Express.js routing engine paired with dynamic EJS server-side rendering.</li>
                    <li><strong>Database:</strong> MongoDB Atlas integration managed through structured Mongoose schemas (Users, Blogs, OTPs).</li>
                    <li><strong>Asset Management:</strong> Dedicated static asset serving, custom dark-mode glassmorphism styling, and responsive layout scaling.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- Footer -->
